    "body": "## Summary\n\n`MainViewModel` creates its shared `SecureRandom` with a fixed seed, `\"75rgu86gr59ht86\"`. While I was exercising the app with the dynamic-analysis tool `ape`, its `SecureRandom` check reported that this seed does not come from a random source.\n\nOn current Android providers a seed passed to the constructor is mixed into the generator's state rather than replacing it, so the generated file names are not predictable today. Still, a hard-coded seed adds no randomness and would make the output predictable on any provider that uses the seed as given. This change lets the platform seed the generator.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `app/src/main/java/rocks/poopjournal/metadataremover/viewmodel/MainViewModel.kt`: `SecureRandom(\"75rgu86gr59ht86\".toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8))` becomes `SecureRandom()`. The file-name alphabet, length and every use of `random` stay the same.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\nThe changed file compiles (`:app:compileDebugKotlin`). I could not complete `assembleDebug` locally: it stops at `:app:hiltJavaCompileDebug` on the unmodified `development` branch as well, so that failure is unrelated to this change.\n\n## Additional context\n\nI'm an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI'm happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project's architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers' recommendations.\n",
